WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:15.300 align:start position:0%
 
will you please join me in prayer  Oh God may the words of my mouth and the  meditations of each of our hearts be  acceptable in your sight O God you are a  rock and our Redeemer amen so who has  authority in your life what sources do  you consult for the truth when you have  a question or a problem the answers you  give today are definitely different than  the answers we would have heard 50 or  100 years ago  I think we're far less trusting of  Authority these days and for good reason  the problem also today is that we have  so many voices telling us what to  believe that we just may be more  confused than ever if there is a  question on your mind where do you go  for answers my very unscientific made-up  study says that 48% of you would go to  Google really 25% of you might ask a  friend maybe 10% of you would ask a  family member maybe 17% of you would  consult some authoritative texts on the  question sifting through those options  for yourself of course it depends what  the dilemma is what the question is you  have in mind but think about the sources  of authoritative information in your  life the number of possible sources is  so huge we are more confused than ever  and if the question is a matter of faith  some deep theological question where do  you go  do you pray about it do you read  theologians do you flip through your  Bible do you google it what do we do  when this staggering number of sources  leaves us more confused than ever before  on the one hand we are understandably  skeptical of Authority it's hard to know  who we can trust but even more we want  to find the answers ourselves on the  other hand I think we do share a deep  deep longing for a guide we can trust  through this maze of life if you haven't  noticed the Gospel of Mark is off to an  incredibly fast start it begins with a  few memorable lines about John the  Baptist proclaiming the coming of Christ  only three verses on the baptism of  Jesus two verses covering Jesus forty  days of fasting and temptation in the  wilderness  a few quick verses of Jesus calling the  disciples follow me okay no time for  questions marks in a hurry so our gospel  passage today is only a few paragraphs  into mark and here mark spends more time  on Jesus teaching in the synagogue and  an exorcism than he has on most anything  else so far in his gospel jesus walks  into the gospel into the synagogue and  begins teaching he taught as one having  authority  mark says most who spoke in the  synagogue had authority but this Jesus  was different it seems people really  were listening to his teaching astounded  wondering who he was one in particular  knew who Jesus was a man with an unclean  spirit who began yelling at Jesus what  have you to do with us Jesus of Nazareth  have you come here to destroy us I know  who you are the Holy One of God we may  be tempted to label this person's  condition slap on a diagnosis of mental  illness or call security to have him  contained and escorted out chaos is  uncomfortable and chaos around us in  places of worship or anywhere else where  we're supposed to just sit and be quiet  is extra uncomfortable in dismissing  this man we forget that our own spirits  may not be as perfectly clean as we  think as everyone around Jesus is  listening quietly and puzzling over who  he might be this one who we may label as  troubled is actually the one who knows  who Jesus is the  with the unclean spirit calls Jesus the  Holy One of God  and faced with a wild man yelling at him  Jesus does not run away from this chaos  nor does Jesus leave this man burdened  by that unclean spirit he calls out that  spirit and sets him free some call this  an exorcism some call this a miracle  mark calls this Jesus teaching Jesus  teaches not only through his words to  the crowd in the synagogue that day but  through his stunning actions he steps  toward the chaos of life instead of  turning away from it  Jesus listens to every voice especially  those that the rest of us would rather  ignore and finally Jesus calls out  whatever is possessing us you probably  don't think you're possessed but really  you've never suffered from deep fear or  greed or workaholism surely not here  consumerism addiction I could go on  these and other unclean spirits are very  much a part of our lives and if you  think this talk of unclean spirits  sounds really out there  I assure you that many among us struggle  and if you find that this is hitting  close to home  I assure you that many around you are  also struggling in the Lord's Prayer we  all pray that God will deliver us from  evil even if we don't quite understand  what this means the thing is our world  is in need of healing we are in need of  healing though it is painful to admit  this and we are also in need of one with  authority whom we can turn to for new  life not a political leader not a  presidential candidate not even a  pastoral leader but the Holy One of God  Jesus Christ only Christ can call out of  us what is chaos  and bring us lasting peace in the poetic  words of Jan Richardson to all that is  chaotic and you let there come silence  let there be a calming of the clamoring  a stilling of the voices that have laid  their claim on you that have made their  home in you that go with you even to the  holy places but will not let you rest  will not let you hear your life with  wholeness or feel the grace that  fashioned you let what distracts you  cease let what divides you cease let  there come an end to what diminishes and  demeans and let depart all that keeps  you in its cage let there be an opening  in the quiet that lies beneath the chaos  where you find the peace you did not  think possible and see what shimmers  within the storm if we dare to admit  that we are in need of this this kind of  peace we may be considered weak by our  peers and questioned by our loved ones  if we dare to admit that we cannot find  our way completely on our own which is  why I think most of us are here this  morning then it is possible that Christ  is already transforming your life slowly  calling out of you those things which  hold you captive slowly melting our  hearts of stone and giving us hearts of  flesh that will break open to care for  others if we dare to recognize the one  with the unclean spirit as ourselves  then we too may just be able to say that  Jesus is in fact the Holy One of God  that Christ can in fact make us new  crazy absolutely true  I guess I'm banking my life on it the  uncertainties of our days are many many  and when we've searched for answers long  enough without finding clarity or peace  Jesus meets us right there in the chaos  and the confusion Christ knows what is  consuming our lives and has the power to  transform us as we question authority  and wonder what to believe and grasp for  anything that is certain in this world  Jesus reminds us that truth can be found  even in the chaos the chaos of an infant  born in a barn far far from home the  chaos struggle with whatever is  consuming our lives the chaos of the  cross the chaos of those who discover  the empty tomb on Easter morning the  chaos of Christ rearranging our  carefully made plans and loosening our  grip on our will if you try to live with  Christ as the main authority figure in  your life  I promise you it will be uncomfortable  there will be chaos there will be doubt  and more questions it might be funny  sometimes but it will not always be fun  and I promise that sometimes God will  pry you from a place where you are  comfortable and happy and send you on  your way to someplace else just when you  think who we made it okay let's put down  some roots here for a while longer God  will speak to you as God did long ago we  hear in Deuteronomy  you have stayed long enough at this  mountain continue on your journey it  breaks in my heart to say goodbye to you  and this is because it has been a deep  privilege to serve you for  five-and-a-half years  Ian promised this would be a three  hankie service but I am excited what's  ahead for Jeff and me and I'm excited  what's ahead for this church God is  sending us off this holy mountain to  another place God is sending you to  another place too and that's not because  I'm leaving it's not it's because God is  always always calling us forward and  onward and home

